# Allow-list build context: deny everything, then re-allow only what the image needs
# (deploy/Dockerfile copies: root lock + pyproject, contract/, api/, artifacts/).
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!contract/
!api/
!artifacts/

# --- explicit denials (defence in depth: these win over the allow-list above) ---
# Notebook project, datasets, training state, Keras/Pickle model formats (never deserialised by the API)
notebook
**/data
**/mlruns
**/*.keras
**/*.h5
**/*.pkl
**/*.pickle
**/*.joblib

# Tests, caches, virtualenvs, docs, tooling, VCS
**/tests
**/conftest.py
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.coverage*
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov
.git
.github
deploy
docs
tools

# Secrets and local environment
secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/kaggle.json
